> What is the best way to kill Asmodeus or is it not really necessary?

There's an ascension run trick that involves tossing the amulet to a
covetous monster and letting him carry it for you.  It works with any
demon lord, but Asmodeus is the most convenient one since he's about
the most harmless of them all.  Since you don't really _need_ to kill
him, that could be a good reason to leave him alive (and unbribed).

It does work: I just tried it in wizmode.  It does take a bit of skill
(and preferably a stethoscope), since you need to beat him down to one
third of his hit points to make him escape upstairs while making sure
he stays alive.  (Don't use your main weapon -- hit him with a very
dull knife or something instead.  But do it only _after_ he's got the
amulet, since he won't pick it up if his HPs are low even if you toss
it at him(!).)

The advantage is that you don't suffer the effects of carrying the
amulet, and are spared the wizard's direct attention.  Also, while the
mysterious force affects monsters too, they only get sent down one
level (and will promptly escape back up as soon as you follow them
down).  The disadvantage is that you can get really tired of watching
a demon lord's back end, and that it can be hard to keep him alive
especially if the wizard shows up.

You'll also likely get to meet the lairless demon lords if you hang
around one of their buddies long enough; that's a good reason to use a
lawful demon like Asmodeus as your carrier, since chaotic demon lords
may summon Demogorgon, who's never a pleasant encounter.  Compared to
him, Geryon and Dispater are pretty tame.

Also, the normal way of driving him upstairs won't work in the Valley.
If you don't want to kill him there, you'll need to get the amulet off
him by either stoning and unstoning him or by polying into a nymph and
stealing it off him.  Then lead him upstairs like you'd lead a pet.


