The canonical demonslaying combo is Grayswandir #twoweaponed with an
ordinary silver saber.  Both should be blessed and enchanted for
maximal effectiveness.  Alternatively, silver daggers (also blessed
and enchanted, of course) make excellent distance weapons for Valks,
assuming you can find any.  You _have_ #enhanced dagger to expert,
haven't you?

Remember that all demons respect the E-word, though it won't stop them
from attacking you from a distance.  Writing the E-word on the up
stairs and either dropping an item there or standing there yourself
will prevent him from escaping, and will let you easily finish him
off.  (The same trick works on the Quest, if you haven't done that
yet.)

In my current game (the one in which I blew up a BoH containing
Grayswandir and a wand of wishing in Orcustown) as a lawful Valk I
even spent a wish on an ordinary athame, just for engraving, before
exploring Gehennom.  It's faster than using a gem, more reliable than
using one's fingers and saves on wand charges.

